CM_ BO_ 409 "Status output from the MITM pedal module (TX ~10 Hz). dat[0]=BMW pedal in %, dat[1]=output after max/cut/fault %, dat[2]=state.";
CM_ BO_ 512 "Cruise-control gas request (OP -> pedal). 4 bytes, >=20 Hz, 100 ms timeout -> passthrough. Only ADDS throttle: out=max(bmw_pedal, can_gas). 0% = Tesla unpressed = one-pedal regen. Do not copy Toyota interceptor layout (Toyota 0x200 is 6 bytes).";
CM_ BO_ 513 "Torque-cut / brake override from VCU (3 bytes, 200 ms timeout). Firmware bitfield, NOT magic 90. Panda must not TX 0x201 in v1.";
CM_ BO_ 168 "VCU BMW_E90.cpp SendAbsDscMessages. Live brake on this car. Byte7 BrakeMagic: 0x64 pressed, 0x04 released. Period ~10 ms. e9x EngineAndBrake 0x168 is ICE DME and must not be used for OP brake.";
CM_ BO_ 690 "Live layout is i3LIM Measurement (8 bytes). VCU i3LIM.cpp handle2B2. Conflicting Tesla PCS ChargePowerRequest (5 bytes: ChargerPower 0|16@1+ factor 0.001 kW, ChargerEnable byte2 0x02/0x00) is unused on this DBC; same ID cannot have two layouts.";
CM_ BO_ 932 "Reconstructed. Source DBC truncated at 'BO_ 932 PCS_AlertMatrix_From_PCS: 8 PCSO_ 409'. PCS firmware 0x3A4: byte0 low nibble is page mux; bits 4..63 are live alert bits (page 0 = alerts 1..60, page 1 = 61..120). Original per-alert Tesla names were not recovered.";
CM_ BO_ 1022 "Parking brake status. Byte0 == 2 engaged (plan 0x3FE).";

CM_ SG_ 409 PedalInPct "Normalized BMW pedal input 0-100 %.";
CM_ SG_ 409 PedalOutPct "Final command after cruise/cut/fault 0-100 %.";
CM_ SG_ 409 PedalState "0 PASSTHROUGH, 1 THROTTLEGATING (cut/fault), 2 DRIVEBYWIRE.";
CM_ SG_ 512 GasReq "Raw byte 0-255 = 0-100 %. Factor 100/255.";
CM_ SG_ 512 GasEnable "Must be 0xA5 (165) to enable CAN gas. Anything else is ignored.";
CM_ SG_ 512 GasCounter "Low nibble of byte 2, must increment every frame.";
CM_ SG_ 512 GasChecksum "CRC8 poly 0xD5 init 0xFF over bytes 0..2, forward (not Toyota reverse).";
CM_ SG_ 513 REGEN_CUT "Byte0 bit0 (0x01). Sender din_brake. Pedal firmware ignores this bit (forcing 0% would maximize regen).";
CM_ SG_ 513 ALL_TORQUE_CUT "Byte0 bit1 (0x02). Sender neutralPending. Force interceptor output to 0 %.";
CM_ SG_ 513 CutCounter "Low nibble of byte 1, must increment every frame.";
CM_ SG_ 513 CutChecksum "CRC8 poly 0xD5 init 0xFF over bytes 0..1, forward.";
CM_ SG_ 168 BrakeMagic "Byte 7. 0x64 (100) = brake pressed, 0x04 (4) = released. OP brake_pressed iff == 0x64.";
CM_ SG_ 168 Checksum_A8 "BMW sum-fold of bytes 1-7 plus 0xA8.";
CM_ SG_ 168 Counter_A8 "Incrementing counter byte (VCU A81).";
CM_ SG_ 263 DIR_axleSpeed "Rear axle speed, RPM.";
CM_ SG_ 263 DIR_torqueActual "Rear axle torque, Nm.";
CM_ SG_ 263 DIR_torqueCommand "Rear axle torque request, Nm.";
CM_ SG_ 1761 Opmode "0=Off, 1=Run, 2=Preheat";
CM_ SG_ 1761 CompressorState "0=None, 1=Normal, 2=Wait, 3=Fault, 4=SoftStart, 5=SoftShutdown, 15=SNA";
CM_ SG_ 1761 HeatTransferMode "0=Passive, 1=DominantHeating, 2=DominantCooling";
CM_ SG_ 1761 ThermalDemands "Bitmask: 1=CoolCabin, 2=CoolBattery, 4=CoolPowertrain, 8=HeatCabinL, 16=HeatCabinR, 32=HeatBattery, 64=RadiatorDefrost";
CM_ SG_ 1761 HvPower "Compressor electrical power draw estimate, 0.1 kW/count";

